{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on question dd8547d6, identifiers (c+d): yes. The bounded\ninstance cache satisfies item 6 of ruling 70186a25.\n\n\"Reads once and holds\" means once while the instance holds the checked\nbytes. It does not mean one remote read for the life of the room. The\nkind is a function of the genesis, and every reference holds the\ngenesis digest, so a second read after a restart or an eviction gives\nthe same answer or fails its check. No durable copy is needed for\nreplay, and (c+d) adds none: no SQL row, no retained blob, no archive\nexport, no change to the Native reservation ledger.\n\nConditions.\n\n1. The cache holds only bytes that passed the full identity check:\n   entry hash equal to the reference's genesis, and seed digest equal\n   to the scope ID. A failed check caches nothing.\n2. A cold miss whose read fails or times out judges nothing on a guess.\n   The input gets the existing answer for an unavailable dependency,\n   and no refusal is recorded for it.\n3. The bounds are the ones you name: 32 frames and 8 MiB at current\n   entry bounds, keyed by the full SequenceRef. A duplicate read by\n   concurrent cold inputs is accepted. No pending map and no queue.\n4. A cache hit supplies no authority, no Native birth proof and no\n   `from.pin` evidence, as you wrote.\n\nThe witness shows a hit, an eviction with a fresh checked read, and\ncondition 2.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}